          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which chapter holds high blood pressure, and what does that chapter deliberately exclude?",
          "answer": "High blood pressure falls in **Chapter 9, diseases of the circulatory system** (I00 to I99), in the hypertensive-disease block at **I10 to I16**. Essential, or primary, hypertension is code **I10**. The block holds combination codes that join hypertension with heart or kidney disease attributed to it. (Source: *ICD-10-CM Chapter 9: diseases of the circulatory system*; *Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family*.)\n\nThe retrieved passages do not say what Chapter 9 deliberately excludes. None of them has an exclusions section for that chapter, so I can't answer that part from this evidence.\n\nTwo related points came up. A high blood-pressure reading in someone with no hypertension diagnosis is classified under the symptoms chapter (R00 to R09), not as hypertension (*ICD-10-CM Chapter 18: symptoms, signs and abnormal findings*). Also, the older split between benign and malignant hypertension was not carried into the current system (*Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family*).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
